    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my 2018 honda civic is making this really loud squealing noise whenever i'm accelerating. i think it's coming from the engine area. can you explain what the serpentine belt actually does and why a bad one would make that sound?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The serpentine belt is a single, continuous belt that loops around your engine's pulleys to power essential accessories like the alternator, power steering pump, and AC compressor. A badly worn belt will often develop cracks or glazing on its edges, which creates the loud squealing noise you are hearing as it slips against the pulleys under load. This is especially likely with your 2018 Civic if the belt is overdue for replacement, as older rubber becomes brittle and loses its grip despite the car's age being relatively recent. Ignoring this noise can lead to a loss of all electrical and AC functions if the belt snaps completely while driving.",
      "source": "target",
