    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay that makes sense. i've just noticed that sometimes the noise happens totally randomly, even when i haven't been driving hard, almost like it's just \"glitching\" or something. is there any way it could be an electrical issue acting up like a gremlin in the system or is it always going to be a physical part wearing out?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While a \"gremlin\" or electrical glitch is unlikely to cause the sound itself, the noise you hear is almost certainly a physical mechanical problem, not a software error. The serpentine belt is directly connected to mechanical components, so a squeal usually means the belt is stretching, the tensioner is weak, or a pulley is rusted, all of which wear out physically over time. Even if the issue happens randomly, it stems from this physical degradation becoming severe enough to slip only during certain acceleration patterns or vibration states.",
